00:17:55.700 --> 00:18:02.740
No, it, I actually didn't get far enough to, to, to actually get into this fight.

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:13.160
I just watched a video of it and I'm, I'm glad I did because the game, like, okay, just, just moving away from this fight real quick.

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:20.520
You, you do this, what, what might just describe this loop like five times until you finally get to this boss.

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:23.400
And those five times you're doing the exact same thing.

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:31.600
You're finding, you're, you're finding the supplies, you're, you're buying the pass, you're doing the, the, like, arena mode.

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:32.820
And then you get to this.

00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:35.720
So the, the payoff really isn't there.

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:41.060
The, the guy is obviously based off of Lord Humongous, uh, at least with the mask.

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:43.560
And I guess he's got, like, crossbows.

00:18:43.780 --> 00:18:45.640
Now you have a crossbow, don't know why.

00:18:45.800 --> 00:18:52.600
But it's really, um, to make that like a mini game to end the game is, is, is very silly.

00:18:52.600 --> 00:18:53.880
It's always very silly.

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:57.200
You touched on a pet peeve of mine there, Sean, but it is true.

00:18:57.700 --> 00:19:04.840
Uh, the, these early games don't get a pass on like the, you suddenly have a weapon that you never had before.

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:10.020
And it's like, you could have at least made the fifth stage of the wasteland.

00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:13.400
You have to like buy the crossbow to move on.

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:15.900
Right. They could have at least like narratively done it that way.

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:27.020
Right. Or put it in a cut scene, an explanation, but to just like, yeah, to just no introduction, you're just dropped into a fight and you could never shoot anybody while you were, uh, or sorry.

00:19:27.260 --> 00:19:30.280
Um, you never had to shoot anybody in like the game.

00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:33.700
Didn't look like that in the, in any of the other modes.

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:39.060
And now all of a sudden it's this, like you said, mini game, it just feels like a really random ending.

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:53.720
Whereas I would have thought, uh, you know, make it like some crazy, much larger vehicle that you have to like somehow knock off and take off in the arena in like a one V one would have been more suitable to like what the game was throwing down.

00:19:53.720 --> 00:20:03.220
Because the game focuses so hard on the vehicle aspects of it that it feels kind of weird to just be like, and at the end, you know, um, the interceptor is nothing.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:06.080
And Max is, uh, is, is behind it all.

00:20:07.780 --> 00:20:16.160
I'd say if it was sort of like a smaller arena, because those arena levels are massive for no reason.

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:25.880
Uh, and then, but it's sort of like those maps that like those matches that you play throughout the game, but they just gave you like the dynamite back.

00:20:26.060 --> 00:20:40.440
And maybe the, the, the final bosses vehicle has some different kind of weapon that you have to like, it's, it's within the abilities of this game to do that.

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:49.100
Um, like just like, it's not like you have to change the generation of video game system for that to be a possibility.

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:52.620
Like in some instances where we recommend something different.

00:20:52.840 --> 00:20:55.140
Uh, yeah, it's just a weird decision.

