00:23:24.600 --> 00:23:34.840
So they were able to, like, like, Immortan Joe is named, um, this is, like, one of his sons that, like, is the main villain in this one.

00:23:35.360 --> 00:23:37.760
Um, the war boys are all there.

00:23:38.260 --> 00:23:44.420
Uh, there's a lot of, it's, it's basically the same map that they reference a lot of the places in the newer games.

00:23:44.420 --> 00:23:56.620
So it's, it's that, um, and I'd say it's a flawed game, but it's actually a really, I'd say it's a fun game and they actually nail, uh, vehicular combat pretty well.

00:23:57.200 --> 00:24:00.340
Um, so I'd say it's, it's overlooked sometime.

00:24:00.720 --> 00:24:02.140
Huh. That's cool.

00:24:02.140 --> 00:24:17.780
And, and I only have one interesting thing to add just because I'm skimming the development page for it, uh, is that it, uh, it was originally, like, George Miller was involved in, like, a true tie-in Mad Max video game.

00:24:17.920 --> 00:24:21.720
But then, I guess, either left the project or, uh.

00:24:21.720 --> 00:24:22.820
Yeah, he didn't like where it was going.

00:24:23.080 --> 00:24:24.080
Yeah, right, left the project.

00:24:24.280 --> 00:24:29.080
But then, like, so this game is, is not that game that he was working on?

00:24:29.080 --> 00:24:31.520
Or you think, like, no, it's not.

00:24:31.800 --> 00:24:34.440
Okay, cool. It's technically the same title.

00:24:34.720 --> 00:24:42.480
Like, I mean, as much as a game that goes through so many iterations and is in development hell for a long time can be the same game.

00:24:42.580 --> 00:24:49.400
Like, it's technically the same, uh, like, continuous development.

00:24:49.720 --> 00:24:54.940
But no, this is not the game that was, like, it didn't have the feature set that that game would have had.

00:24:55.240 --> 00:24:56.260
Got it, got it.

00:24:56.920 --> 00:24:57.780
Very interesting.

00:24:57.780 --> 00:24:59.260
Very surprising, I do.

00:24:59.420 --> 00:25:05.800
I think Mad Max is certainly one of those, uh, that lends itself to video game adaptations.

00:25:06.040 --> 00:25:10.200
But so would, uh, like, the Terminator franchise, right?

00:25:10.300 --> 00:25:12.620
And you don't see, like, too many Terminator games.

00:25:13.060 --> 00:25:14.760
Like, they exist, but there's not, like.

00:25:14.880 --> 00:25:16.160
Yeah, they're not good.

00:25:16.760 --> 00:25:20.700
Yeah, or, yeah, or it's just not, like, as, as many as you would think.

00:25:20.700 --> 00:25:28.860
Like, I think there's a lot of these 80s action movies that the NES, like, was almost, like, obligated to have.

00:25:28.860 --> 00:25:35.360
Because they were, you know, at the time, like, they were expected to, you know, break off from the movie, release a video game.

00:25:35.620 --> 00:25:37.300
Fans of the movie would then buy the game.

00:25:37.300 --> 00:25:39.360
And it's just, like, another revenue stream.

00:25:39.860 --> 00:25:43.220
That's not, like, true, though, of, like, oh, well, then we also have to do that.

00:25:43.500 --> 00:25:45.400
