00:26:35.240 --> 00:26:39.200
And that is whether Mad Max will be on the Essential Games list.

00:26:42.480 --> 00:26:48.680
As far as movie tie-in video games go, this is pretty solid.

00:26:48.680 --> 00:26:55.660
I do feel like it's mostly inspired slash connected to the movie franchise.

00:26:55.660 --> 00:26:59.060
And I can tell that that's the Interceptor.

00:26:59.060 --> 00:27:02.300
And I can follow with the vehicular combat stuff.

00:27:02.600 --> 00:27:09.500
What I can't get over is just that the gameplay loop itself is pretty stale after the first time you do it.

00:27:09.500 --> 00:27:20.320
It's a little disappointing to not have, like, one giant wasteland that you kind of explore, backtrack through when you, you know, buy new stuff at a shop.

00:27:20.500 --> 00:27:23.540
You know, like, not Metroid, but kind of Metroid-y.

00:27:24.100 --> 00:27:25.160
Something like that.

00:27:25.300 --> 00:27:32.080
And instead just being like, no, it's just like we gated off the next section of the wasteland that looks exactly like this section.

00:27:32.360 --> 00:27:37.740
But just, you know, we moved some buildings and changed the directions of the roads.

00:27:37.740 --> 00:27:44.060
I just, I can't, I can't in good conscience say that that's a smart design choice for a video game.

00:27:45.640 --> 00:27:56.980
So while I like how connected this feels to the franchise itself, probably even more than Gilligan's Island, which was also feeling pretty good as, like, as far as franchise games go.

00:27:56.980 --> 00:28:11.640
So I think video game developers in general right now are learning the right lessons about, like, not doing the back to the future thing of just, like, yeah, if you just, like, loosely tell the story and make gameplay elements around those story beats, you'll have a great movie video game.

00:28:11.700 --> 00:28:13.140
It's like, no, that's not the way to do it.

00:28:13.180 --> 00:28:16.320
But this isn't necessarily the way to go either.

00:28:16.320 --> 00:28:22.320
You can't just lay down some great ideas but not follow through on the full experience.

00:28:23.160 --> 00:28:25.100
There's not a full experience to this game.

00:28:25.260 --> 00:28:28.180
And so for that reason, it won't be on the Essential Games list for me.

